remstart
    THE GUIDE
    the angler, at work in the first dive. in angler_run it brings the dark down and the game stops until
    it has gone. here there is no dark, it sits under the board in a box of its own, and the player
    goes on playing while it talks. the routines are in fish_routines_guide.

    it uses the pictures, the box, the words and the voice of the angler, so only one of the two can be
    up at a time. angler_run sends the guide away if it ever comes while the guide is up.

    guide_enter is how it first shows up, and it is the only part that holds the game back. the line
    of text comes up on its own, a small light comes on down in the deep, the angler swims up behind
    it, a "!" pops up over its head, and it cuts the line off.

    from then on, guideSay() has it say something now, and guideThen() has it say something once the
    words before have had time to be read. neither one waits for a button, and neither one holds up a
    swap. guideLeave() has it swim off.

    the whole board has no room under it. guideAside() takes it across the board while the board comes in,
    and guideBeside() brings the box back, in the column under the codec, and it turns around to face
    the board. the panels of info mode about the rounds and the codec would come down over it, so they
    go to the left of what they are about while it is there. see layoutInfoPanel.

    it knows a lot, and it will teach the player, but it wants them to relax first: calm down, no rush,
    it will tell them soon. it talks slowly, and it says more than the rules. the board does not move on
    until it has finished: see guideReady.

    it listens, too. what it says depends a little on what the player does on the little boards, and
    the tutorial keeps track of that here. see tutorialMissed, tutorial_pop and tutorialWatch.

    guideVisit() has it swim up to one thing around the board, with an outline on it, to talk about that
    and nothing else. guideVisitEnd() sends it back to where it talks from. see tutorial_visit.
remend

global GUIDE_ON = 0 `1 while the angler is up as the guide. frame_guide does nothing until it is.
global GUIDE_LEAVING = 0 `1 while it swims off
global GUIDE_GLOW_TWEEN_ID = 0 `how much of its light has come on, from 0 to 1
global GUIDE_BOX_TWEEN_ID = 0 `how much of the box can be seen, from 0 to 1
global GUIDE_BANG_TWEEN_ID = 0 `the "!" over its head, from 0 to 1 and back
global GUIDE_BANG_TEXT_ID = 0

` where it talks from. the three rows in the middle of the board end at 218, and the hints start at 304.
global GUIDE_BOX_X = 150
global GUIDE_BOX_Y = 236
global GUIDE_BOX_H = 56

` where it talks from once the whole board is in. the box is narrow there, so what it says there is short.
global GUIDE_SIDE = 0 `1 while it talks from there
global GUIDE_SIDE_TWEEN_ID = 0 `how far across it has got, from 0 to 1
global GUIDE_SIDE_X = 438
global GUIDE_SIDE_Y = 92
global GUIDE_SIDE_BOX_X = 426
global GUIDE_SIDE_BOX_Y = 158
global GUIDE_SIDE_BOX_W = 138
global GUIDE_SIDE_BOX_H = 140
global GUIDE_CROSS_MS = 1300 `how long it takes to get across

` the one thing that it is talking about. see guideVisit.
global GUIDE_VISITING = 0 `1 while it is up there
global GUIDE_VISIT_TWEEN_ID = 0 `how far it has got, from 0 to 1
global GUIDE_VISIT_X = 0
global GUIDE_VISIT_Y = 0
global GUIDE_VISIT_MS = 1100 `how long it takes to get there

` where it starts from, from where it ends up, and how small it is out there
global GUIDE_DEEP_X = -34
global GUIDE_DEEP_Y = 40
global GUIDE_DEEP_SCALE# = .45

` when things happen in guide_enter, in milliseconds from when the line of text starts
global GUIDE_LIGHT_AT = 1800
global GUIDE_SWIM_AT = 4400
global GUIDE_BANG_AT = 7400
global GUIDE_TALK_AT = 8600
global GUIDE_LIGHT_MS = 2200 `how long the light takes to come on
global GUIDE_ENTER_MS = 2800 `how long it takes to swim up, the first time
global GUIDE_RISE_MS = 900 `how long it takes to swim off
global GUIDE_BANG_MS = 700 `how long the "!" is up
global GUIDE_HOLD_MS = 2800 `how long words stay up once they have been said, before what comes next

` the words that are waiting to be said. see guideThen.
global GUIDE_QUEUE_ROOM = 6
global dim GUIDE_QUEUE$(6)
global GUIDE_QUEUED = 0
global GUIDE_NEXT_MS = 0 `when the next words are said, or 0 until the words before are all out
global GUIDE_QUIET_MS = 0 `when everything that it said has had time to be read, or 0 until it has stopped. see guideReady.

` what the player has done on the little boards, for what the angler says about it
global TUTORIAL_SWAPS = 0 `the swaps on this board that popped nothing
global TUTORIAL_VISIT = 0 `what it swims up to before the next board. see tutorial_visit.
global TUTORIAL_RETRY = 0 `1 when the last board popped, where it should have been a school, and it comes in again
global TUTORIAL_SCHOOLS_WAS = 0 `SCHOOL_COUNT when this board came in, to see if it made a school
global TUTORIAL_BOARD_MS = 0 `when this board came in
global TUTORIAL_IDLE_MS = 0 `when anything was last pressed
global TUTORIAL_WAIT_SAID = 0 `1 once it has told the player that there is no rush, on this board
global TUTORIAL_IDLE_LIMIT = 15000 `how long the player can sit there before it says so
global TUTORIAL_QUICK_MS = 14000 `a school that takes less than this is quick
global TUTORIAL_INFO_TRIES = 0 `how many times the info key has been pressed too soon

` its last words of the tutorial. see tutorial_goodbye.
global GUIDE_END_TALK = 0 `1 while it says them, and it goes when they are done
global GUIDE_MARK_NEXT = 0 `when the next question mark comes up
global GUIDE_MARKS_UNTIL = 0 `when the last question mark will have gone, or 0 when there are none up




























